WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:02.517
Open Disaster Recovery from Operations.

00:00:02.859 --> 00:00:06.869
Add or review the datacenter, its Foundation endpoint and dependency

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:07.659
reviews.

00:00:07.979 --> 00:00:11.136
Link a complete Foundation V M configuration and the cluster

00:00:11.349 --> 00:00:14.199
post-configuration pipeline to a recovery profile.

00:00:14.361 --> 00:00:17.454
Use existing cluster to rebuild for re-foundation.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:20.078
Recovery reconstructs infrastructure.

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:24.089
Restoring virtual machines and applications remains the responsibility of

00:00:24.131 --> 00:00:26.031
your backup and recovery platform.

00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:30.257
Review Profile shows the captured deployment and pipeline snapshots.

00:00:30.556 --> 00:00:35.334
Check the exact cluster name, address, physical node serials, images,

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.168
networks and every configuration step.

00:00:38.484 --> 00:00:42.210
The status is calculated from the latest revision and its source files.

00:00:42.751 --> 00:00:47.146
Baseline changed means a source file, pipeline or datacenter Foundation

00:00:47.316 --> 00:00:50.505
endpoint no longer matches the reviewed snapshot.

00:00:50.792 --> 00:00:55.230
To adopt the intended current settings, choose Capture New Revision, save

00:00:55.315 --> 00:01:00.008
the draft, inspect its targets, enter Baseline review notes and select Mark

00:01:00.136 --> 00:01:01.257
Baseline Reviewed.

00:01:01.525 --> 00:01:05.123
Marking the old snapshot reviewed does not clear a continuing mismatch.

00:01:05.493 --> 00:01:09.248
Capture New Revision is the current profile editing path and retains earlier

00:01:09.418 --> 00:01:10.101
revisions.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.119
The current interface has no profile delete action.

00:01:13.492 --> 00:01:15.967
Baseline review does not image hardware.

00:01:16.223 --> 00:01:20.191
Prepare a run only after review, then obtain the separate exact-content

00:01:20.489 --> 00:01:23.305
deployment approval and destructive confirmations.

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:26.332
Deployed rehearsals also make real changes.

00:01:26.925 --> 00:01:30.851
Enter the required cluster and Foundation confirmation phrases, acknowledge

00:01:31.021 --> 00:01:33.091
the imaging scope, and deploy once.

00:01:33.453 --> 00:01:35.837
Follow the linked job and Foundation session.

00:01:36.172 --> 00:01:41.249
A non-JSON response or H T T P four twenty-nine can be a transport or

00:01:41.292 --> 00:01:43.617
rate-limit issue while imaging continues.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:47.415
Inspect the existing job and target state before retrying.

00:01:47.735 --> 00:01:50.968
Stop Orchestration does not prove that Foundation has stopped.

00:01:51.375 --> 00:01:55.641
After confirmed deployment success, use the initial access bootstrap when

00:01:55.684 --> 00:01:59.609
the captured pipeline begins with eligible password and EULA or Pulse

00:01:59.737 --> 00:02:00.292
settings.

00:02:00.548 --> 00:02:04.633
Obtain each required exact-content approval and acknowledge the cluster.

00:02:04.963 --> 00:02:07.886
Run only the permitted narrow bootstrap prefix.

00:02:08.206 --> 00:02:11.747
This removes the need to log in manually just to change the initial password

00:02:11.833 --> 00:02:12.942
before health collection.

00:02:13.326 --> 00:02:16.190
Broader cluster configuration still waits for verification.

00:02:16.714 --> 00:02:20.597
Collect P E Health Readbacks using the reviewed post-bootstrap credential

00:02:20.938 --> 00:02:22.687
and verified certificate trust.

00:02:22.986 --> 00:02:27.338
Check cluster identity, complete expected membership and explicitly reported

00:02:27.466 --> 00:02:27.927
health.

00:02:28.217 --> 00:02:32.761
Missing fields, authentication failures or network errors remain unknown.

00:02:33.081 --> 00:02:37.603
If automatic evidence is unavailable, independently verify P E and record

00:02:37.859 --> 00:02:40.306
the manual attestation with its evidence reference.

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:44.090
Begin remaining configuration within fifteen minutes of fresh evidence.

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:47.703
Run the remaining eligible steps from the captured snapshots.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:52.439
If a step fails, reconcile actual state and continue only the unfinished

00:02:52.609 --> 00:02:53.127
work.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:58.295
Where approval policy requires a direct job, run the exact approved snapshot

00:02:58.465 --> 00:03:01.196
and link its successful job to the pending step.

00:03:01.537 --> 00:03:04.769
Do not repeat successful imaging or password changes.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:09.110
Finish with independent acceptance and an explicit handoff to the backup

00:03:09.153 --> 00:03:11.195
platform for workload restoration.
